{{also|Buddy}}
==English==
{{wikipedia|dab=buddy}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/bʌd.i/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-buddy.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌdi}}

===Etymology 1===
1802, colloquial {{m|en|butty||companion}}, also the form of an older dialect term meaning [[workmate]], associated with coal mining. Itself believed derived from 1530 as ''booty fellow'', a partner with whom one shares booty or loot.<ref>{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary|accessdate=November 2008}}</ref> Alternatively, an alteration of {{m|en|brother}}.<ref>{{R:Lexico}}</ref><ref>{{R:Merriam-Webster Online}}</ref>

====Noun====
{{en-noun|buddies}}

# A [[friend]] or [[casual]] acquaintance.
#: {{syn|en|mate|Thesaurus:friend}}
#: {{ux|en|They have been '''buddies''' since they were in school.}}
# A [[partner]] for a particular activity.
#: {{ux|en|drinking '''buddies'''}}
# An [[informal]] and friendly address to a [[stranger]]; a friendly [[placeholder]] name for a person one does not know.
#: {{syn|en|mate|fellow}}
#: {{ux|en|Hey, '''buddy''', I think you dropped this.}}

